+Reading from a file
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Use :meth:`~rich.progress.Progress.open` to read a file while a progress bar advances with the number of bytes read. The module-level :func:`~rich.progress.open` manages its own display, so the bar is shown while the ``with`` block is active::
+
+    import rich.progress
+
+    with rich.progress.open("data.json") as f:
+        data = f.read()
+
+The default mode is ``'r'``, which yields text. Use ``'rb'`` to receive bytes instead::
+
+    import rich.progress
+
+    with rich.progress.open("data.bin", "rb") as f:
+        data = f.read()
+
+If no ``total`` is given, the total is the size of the file in bytes. Pass ``total`` to override it.
+
+Reading from a file-like object
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+If you already have an open binary file, use the module-level :func:`~rich.progress.wrap_file`, which manages its own display. Only binary files are supported, and ``total`` is required. The reader does not close the wrapped file, so it remains open after the ``with`` block::
+
+    import rich.progress
+
+    with open("data.bin", "rb") as f:
+        with rich.progress.wrap_file(f, total=1024) as reader:
+            data = reader.read()
+        # f is still open here
+
